{% comment %}
  Upcoming events. The buy point of the seminars page.

  TWO SOURCES, and the collection wins when it is set.

    collection   one row per product, everything read from metafields
    blocks       hand-authored rows, used when no collection is chosen

  Blocks are the fallback rather than the primary because a typed price is a
  lie waiting to happen: it sits next to a real product and does not follow it.
  A dead product handle behaves the same way -- Liquid returns nothing rather
  than erroring, so the row silently falls back to typed values and looks
  perfectly normal. That has already happened once here, when a product was
  renamed. In collection mode the product is the only source, so a missing one
  is a missing row.

  THE SETTING IS `events_collection`, NOT `collection`. A setting whose id is
  `collection` collides with Liquid's global collection drop and reads back
  EMPTY -- `section.settings.collection` is blank however valid the template
  JSON is. Nothing errors; the section just falls through to the blocks branch
  and renders plausible-looking rows from the wrong source. Do not rename it
  back. The same caution applies to `product`, `cart` and `customer`.

  METAFIELDS, all on the product, all namespace `custom`:

    custom_seminar_city    single line text   "Tampa, FL"
    custom_seminar_start   date               2026-09-25
    custom_seminar_end     date               2026-09-26
    custom_seminar_focus   single line text   "Upper Body", blank = TBA

  The displayed date is DERIVED from start and end, so nobody types
  "September 25 & 26" and nobody can mistype it. Same month collapses to
  "September 25 & 26"; different months render both.

  SORTING. Liquid cannot sort a collection by a metafield -- `sort` reaches
  simple properties only. So the rows are ordered by building an array of
  `YYYYMMDD~index` strings and sorting THAT: the key is zero-padded and
  fixed-width, which makes a lexical sort chronological. The loop index rather
  than the handle avoids `all_products`, which is capped at 20 lookups a page.

  A product with no start date sorts last on 99999999 rather than jumping to
  the front on an empty key.

  PAST EVENTS DROP OFF by themselves, judged on the end date so a seminar is
  still listed on its first morning. Nothing has to be remembered.

  WHERE THE ROW GOES. A row is an <a>, and an <a> cannot contain the <form>
  that a true "straight to checkout" needs, so there are two honest options:
  the product page, or /cart/{variant}:1. Neither lands the buyer on checkout.
  The note under the list says "straight to secure checkout"; if that copy is
  kept, this needs rebuilding as one form per row with a submit styled as the
  row, which costs the whole-row click target. Flagged rather than quietly
  mismatched.

  ELEMENT. The root is a <div>: `"tag": "section"` already wraps this.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign anchor = section.settings.anchor | handle
  assign events = section.settings.events_collection
  assign today = 'now' | date: '%Y%m%d' | plus: 0
-%}

<div class="suf-section" {% if anchor != blank %}id="{{ anchor }}"{% endif %}>
  <div class="suf-wrap">
    <div class="suf-semlist">
      {%- if events != blank -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign keyed = ''
          for p in events.products
            assign starts = p.metafields.custom.custom_seminar_start.value | date: '%Y%m%d'
            if starts == blank
              assign starts = '99999999'
            endif
            assign keyed = keyed | append: starts | append: '~' | append: forloop.index0 | append: ','
          endfor
          assign keys = keyed | split: ',' | sort
          assign shown = 0
        -%}

        {%- for key in keys -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign idx = key | split: '~' | last | plus: 0
            assign product = events.products[idx]

            assign starts = product.metafields.custom.custom_seminar_start.value
            assign ends = product.metafields.custom.custom_seminar_end.value | default: starts

            # Judged on the end date, so a two-day seminar is still listed on
            # its first morning.
            #
            # `| plus: 0` on both sides is load-bearing: Liquid compares
            # strings with < by returning false, silently, so an unconverted
            # comparison never drops anything and the filter looks like it
            # works right up until a date passes.
            assign over = ends | date: '%Y%m%d' | plus: 0
            assign is_past = false
            if ends != blank and over < today
              assign is_past = true
            endif
          -%}

          {%- if is_past == false and shown < section.settings.limit -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign shown = shown | plus: 1

              # Each half is formatted on its OWN line. Chaining them --
              # `first | append: ' & ' | append: ends | date: '%-d'` -- pipes
              # the whole concatenated string into date, not the end date.
              assign m1 = starts | date: '%B'
              assign m2 = ends | date: '%B'
              assign first_half = starts | date: '%B %-d'
              if m1 == m2
                assign second_half = ends | date: '%-d'
              else
                assign second_half = ends | date: '%B %-d'
              endif
              assign when = first_half | append: ' & ' | append: second_half
              if starts == blank
                assign when = ''
              endif

              assign city = product.metafields.custom.custom_seminar_city.value | default: product.title
              assign focus = product.metafields.custom.custom_seminar_focus.value
              assign price = product.price | money_without_trailing_zeros

              assign sold_out = false
              unless product.available
                assign sold_out = true
              endunless

              if section.settings.link_mode == 'cart'
                assign vid = product.selected_or_first_available_variant.id
                assign target = '/cart/' | append: vid | append: ':1'
              else
                assign target = product.url
              endif
            -%}

            {%- comment -%}
              Every argument is a plain variable. A render argument takes a
              value, not an expression -- `sold_out: product.available == false`
              is a parse error, and the section 500s rather than degrading.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- render 'suf-semrow',
              city: city,
              date: when,
              focus: focus,
              price: price,
              target: target,
              sold_out: sold_out,
              cue: section.settings.cue
            -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}

      {%- else -%}
        {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign product = block.settings.product
            assign target = block.settings.url
            if target == blank and product != blank
              if block.settings.link_mode == 'cart'
                assign vid = product.selected_or_first_available_variant.id
                assign target = '/cart/' | append: vid | append: ':1'
              else
                assign target = product.url
              endif
            endif

            assign sold_out = false
            if product != blank
              assign price = product.price | money_without_trailing_zeros
              unless product.available
                assign sold_out = true
              endunless
            else
              assign price = block.settings.price
            endif
          -%}

          {%- render 'suf-semrow',
            city: block.settings.city,
            date: block.settings.date,
            focus: block.settings.focus,
            price: price,
            target: target,
            sold_out: sold_out,
            cue: block.settings.cue,
            attrs: block.shopify_attributes
          -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- if section.settings.note != blank -%}
      <div class="suf-semnote">{% render 'suf-nb', text: section.settings.note %}</div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Event list (SUF)",
  "tag": "section",
  "max_blocks": 20,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "anchor",
      "label": "Anchor id",
      "info": "Lets a button elsewhere link here, e.g. \"upcoming\"."
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Source" },
    {
      "type": "collection",
      "id": "events_collection",
      "label": "Seminars collection",
      "info": "Set this and the rows come from its products. City, dates and focus are read from each product's metafields; the Event blocks below are then ignored."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "limit",
      "label": "Rows to show",
      "min": 1,
      "max": 12,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 6
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "link_mode",
      "label": "Where Reserve goes",
      "info": "Collection mode only. Neither lands directly on checkout -- see the section comment.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "product", "label": "Product page" },
        { "value": "cart", "label": "Add to cart, then cart" }
      ],
      "default": "product"
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cue", "label": "Link text", "default": "Reserve" },
    { "type": "richtext", "id": "note", "label": "Note under the list" }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "event",
      "name": "Event (fallback)",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "city", "label": "City" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "date", "label": "Date" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "focus",
          "label": "Focus",
          "info": "e.g. \"Upper Body\". Leave blank if not announced yet."
        },
        {
          "type": "product",
          "id": "product",
          "label": "Product",
          "info": "Supplies the price, the link and sold-out state."
        },
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "link_mode",
          "label": "Where Reserve goes",
          "options": [
            { "value": "product", "label": "Product page" },
            { "value": "cart", "label": "Add to cart, then cart" }
          ],
          "default": "product"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "price",
          "label": "Price fallback",
          "info": "Only used when no product is selected."
        },
        { "type": "text", "id": "url", "label": "Link override" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "cue", "label": "Link text", "default": "Reserve" }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Event list (SUF)",
      "blocks": [{ "type": "event" }, { "type": "event" }]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
